{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>A feast.</b> A set meal accompanied by wine, wine being something he cherished — as the outcome proved relative to the beginning (Genesis 19:33). But Abraham made no feast except on the day Isaac was weaned (Genesis 21:8), for the great men of the generation who were accustomed to such practices in times of rejoicing, as the Sages of blessed memory stated (Sotah 10): קַמֵּי דְּשָׁתֵי חַמְרָא, חַמְרָא (\"before those who are used to drinking wine, wine [is appropriate]\")."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:43.182211939Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}